hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2641","Ahmad bin Suleiman told me, he said: Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, he said: Thabit bin Qais Al-Ghaffari told me, he said: Abu Saeed told me Al-Maqbari said: Abu Hurairah told me, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to narrate the fast,” and it would be said: No. He breaks the fast, and he breaks the fast and it is said: He does not fast."
"2642","Amr bin Uthman reported, on the authority of Baqiya, saying: Buhair told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Maadan, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, that Aisha She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to fast on Mondays and Thursdays.”"
"2643","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdullah bin Dawud told us, he said: Thawr told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Ma’dan, on the authority of Rabi’ah Al-Jurashi, on the authority of Aisha, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to investigate on Mondays and Thursdays.”"
"2644","Ishaq bin Ibrahim narrated, he said: Ubaid bin Saeed Al-Umawi narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Khalid bin Maadan, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to search on Mondays and Thursdays.”"
"2645","Ahmad bin Suleiman reported, saying: Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Khalid bin Saeed, on the authority of Aisha, She said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to search on Mondays and Thursdays.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is an objectionable hadith, similar to a hadith Mansour, it looks like it came from Abu Dawud (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2646","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Habib bin Al-Shahid reported, saying: Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, on the authority of Al-Khuza’i, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to fast on Mondays and Thursdays.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2647","Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Abu Nasr al-Tamar told me, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of both, on the authority of Umm Salamah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to fast three days every month: the Monday and Thursday of that Friday. And the next two days.”"
"2648","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Ishaq told us, he said: Al-Nadr told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Asim bin Abi Al-Najjoud, on the authority of Likewise, on the authority of Hafsa, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to fast three days of every month: on Thursday, and on Thursday.” Monday of the first Friday, and of the second Friday on Monday.”"
"2649","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria reported, saying: Husayn told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Hafsa, she said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “When he went to bed, he would place his right palm under his right cheek, and he would fast on Mondays and Thursdays.”"
"2650","Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Hasan bin Shaqiq narrated, he said: My father informed us, he said: Abu Hamza narrated, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zar, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Masoud said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to fast for three days on the first day of every month, and he rarely broke his fast on Friday.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This Abu Hamza, whose name is: Muhammad ibn Maymun, is a Marwazi and there is nothing wrong with him, except that his eyesight went missing at the end of the year. His age, so whoever wrote about him before that, his hadith is good, and Abu Hamzah, the companion of Ibrahim al-Nakha’i, his name is: One-eyed Maimun, and he is not trustworthy. Abu Hamza Thabit bin Abi Safiyya is Kufi, and he is not trustworthy, and Abu Hamza Imran bin Abi Ata, he narrates on the authority of Ibn Abbas, Shu'bah, Sufyan, and Abu Awanah narrated on his authority, but he is not strong, and Abu Hamza Talha bin Yazid: Kufi is trustworthy, and Abu Hamza Muhammad bin Ka’b Al-Qurazi is a trustworthy Madani, Abu Hamza Saad, on the authority of Ubaid, Kufi is trustworthy, and Abu Hamza Anas bin Sirin is trustworthy. They are four brothers: Muhammad bin Sirin, Yahya bin Sirin, Ma’abad bin Sirin, Anas bin Sirin, and Hafsa bint Sirin. And Karima bint Sirin, and they are the servants of Anas bin Malik Al-Ansari. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2651","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Abu Kamil told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Asim bin Bahdala, on the authority of a man, On the authority of Al-Aswad bin Hilal, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, commanded me to perform the two rak’ahs of the forenoon prayer, and not go to sleep except after praying Witr. And fasting three days of the month.”"
"2652","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, he heard Ibn Abbas being asked about fasting on the day of Ashura. He said: “ I have never known the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, to fast a day seeking his superiority over other days except this day, meaning Ashura. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2653","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman bin Awf, he said: I heard On the day of Ashura, Muawiyah was on the pulpit, saying: O people of Medina, where are your scholars? O people of Medina, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, he says on this day: “I am fasting, so whoever wants to fast, let him fast.”"
"2654","Zakaria bin Yahya reported, he said: Shayban reported, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Al-Hurr bin Al-Sayyah, on the authority of Hunaida bin Khaled, on the authority of his wife, said: Some of the wives of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told me that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to “fast on Ashura, the ninth of Dhul-Hijjah, and three days of the month: the first Monday of the month, and the two Thursdays.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2655","Ali bin Hajar reported, he said: Ismail reported, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir, on the authority of his brother Mutarrif, On the authority of Imran, he said: It was said: O Messenger of God, so-and-so does not break his fast during the day all the time, so he said: “He neither fasted nor did he break his fast.”"
"2656","Amr bin Hisham told me, he said: Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Mutarrif bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir, he said: My father told me that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioning to him a man who fasts all the time, so he said: “He neither fasts nor breaks his fast.”"
"2657","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: I heard Mutarrif bin Abdullah Ibn al-Shakhir narrates, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said regarding daily fasting: “He shall neither fast nor break his fast.” Mentioning the disagreement over Ghaylan bin Jarir in it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2658","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, he said: Abu Hilal told us, he said: Ghaylan, he is Ibn Jarir, told us. He said: Abdullah bin Ma’abad Al-Zamani told us, on the authority of Abu Qatada, on the authority of Omar, he said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we passed a man They said: O Prophet of God, this man has not broken his fast since so-and-so, so he said: “He neither fasted nor broke his fast, or he neither fasted nor broke his fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2659","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ghaylan bin Jarir, he heard Abdullah bin Ma’bad Al-Zamani, on the authority of Abu Qatada, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about his fasting and he became angry, so Omar said: We are satisfied with God as our Lord. And with Islam as a religion, and with Muhammad as a messenger, and he was asked about someone who fasted all the time, and he said: “He neither fasted nor broke his fast, or he never fasted nor broke his fast.” Mentioning the disagreement over Ata bin Abi Rabah in it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2660","Hajib bin Sulaiman told me, he said: Al-Harith bin Atiyya told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever fasts forever will not fast.”"
"2661","Issa bin Musawar reported, on the authority of Al-Walid, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said: Ata’ told me, on the authority of Abdullah. And Anba Muhammad bin Abdullah said: Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Ata’ told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever fasts forever has neither fasted nor broken his fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2662","Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazyd Al-Biruti told me, he said: My father told me, and Uqba told me, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Ata bin Abi told me. Rabah said: Someone told me who heard Abdullah bin Omar say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever fasts forever will not fast.”"
"2663","Ismail bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Muhammad bin Musa told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of who, he heard Abdullah bin Omar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever fasts forever will not fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2664","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I read from Ahmad bin Ibrahim that Ibn Aidh narrated to them, and he was Muhammad of Damascus. He said: Yahya narrated to us. He is Ibn Hamza, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Ata’, that he narrated to him, saying: He narrated to me who heard Abdullah bin Amr say: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever fasts forever has neither fasted nor broken his fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2665","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, he said: Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: I heard Ata’, that Abu Abbas the poet told him He heard Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas saying: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was informed that I am fasting and praying, and he narrated the hadith. He said: He said: Ataa: I do not know how he mentioned eternal fasting. He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No one fasts who has fasted forever.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu Al-Abbas the poet, his name is Al-Sa’ib bin Farukh, trustworthy, and his son Al-Ala’ bin Abi Al-Abbas narrates the hadith from him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2666","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told me, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that Hamza bin Amr Al-Aslami asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: O Messenger of God, I am a man who loves to fast, should I fast while travelling? He said: “Fast if you want, and break your fast.” \If you wish\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"2667","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ammar, on the authority of Amr ibn Sharhabeel, on the authority of a man from the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: It was said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: A man who fasts all the time. He said: “I wish “He did not feed the time.” They said: “So two-thirds of it?” He said: “More.” They said: Half of it? He said: “More,” then he said: “Shall I not tell you what removes hotness? Fasting for three days of every month.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2668","Muhammad ibn Al-Ala informed us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Abu Ammar, on the authority of Amr ibn Sharhabeel, he said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, what do you say about a man who fasts all the time? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I wish that time did not add anything to time.” He said: Two-thirds of it? He said: “More.” He said: Half of it. He said: “More. Shall I not inform you of what will take away the heart?” They said: Yes. He said: “Fasting for three days.” \from every month\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"2669","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ghailan bin Jarir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ma’abad, on the authority of Abu Qatada, he said: He said Omar: O Messenger of God, what about someone who fasts all the time? He said: “He neither fasted nor broke his fast, or he neither fasted nor broke his fast.” He said: O Messenger of God, what about someone who fasts for two days and breaks his fast one day? He said: “Can anyone bear that?” He said: What about someone who fasts one day and breaks his fast one day? He said: “That was the fast of David.” He said: What about someone who fasts one day and breaks his fast for two days? He said: “I wish I could be able to endure that.” He said: Then he said: “The three days of every month, and Ramadan until this Ramadan is fasting for the whole life.”"
"2670","He said: And while Ahmad bin Mani’ read to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Husayn and Mughirah reported, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abd. God Ibn Amr said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best fast is the fasting of David. He used to fast one day and break his fast the next.”"
"2671","Muhammad bin Muammar told us, he said: Yahya bin Hammad told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: He said: Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas told me: My father married me to a woman of good standing, and he used to go to her and ask her about her husband, and she said: Yes. A man is one of a man. He has not set foot on a bed for us, nor searched for us any belongings since we came to him. He mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: I met him.” So I went with him, and he said: “How do you fast?” I said: Every day. He said: “Fast for three days every Friday.” I said: I am better able to do that. From that, he said: “Fast for two days and break your fast one day.” He said: I am capable of doing better than that. He said: “The best fast is the fasting of David, peace be upon him.” “Fasting one day and breaking the fast the next.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2672","Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Yunus narrated, saying: Abther narrated to us, he said: Husayn narrated to us, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Amr said: My father married me to a woman, and he came to visit her, and he said: How do you see your husband? She said: What a fine man he is from a man who does not sleep at night and does not break his fast during the day. He met me and slept at night, and said: I married you to a Muslim woman. So I held it, and he said: I did not pay attention to what he said because of the strength and diligence I saw in myself. This was conveyed to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “But I get up and sleep, and I fast and break my fast, so get up and sleep, and fast and break my fast.” He said: “Fast for three days every month.” So I said: I am stronger than that. He said: “Fast the fast of David, peace be upon him. Fast one day and break your fast the next.” I said: I am stronger than that. He said: “Read the Qur’an every month,” then he concluded to fifteen, and I say: I am stronger than that. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2673","Yahya bin Durst reported, he said: Abu Ismail reported, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told us, that Abu Salamah told him, Abdullah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered my room and said: “Have I not been informed that you stay up all night and fast during the day?” He said: Yes, he said: “So do not do that. Sleep and get up, fast and break your fast, for your eyes have a right over you, and your body has a right over you, and your wife has a right over you. You have a right upon you, and your guest has a right upon you, and your friend has a right upon you, and it is possible that you will live long, and it is sufficient for you to fast from Three times every month, and that is fasting for a whole life, and a good deed is multiplied ten times more.” I said: I am finding strength, so I strengthened and he strengthened me. He said: Fast for three days every Friday.” I said: I can bear more than that, so I stressed, and he stressed to me. He said: “Fast like the fast of the Prophet of God, David, upon him.” Peace.” I said: What was David’s fast? He said: “Half an eternity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2674","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab told me And Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, that Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas said: It was mentioned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he says I will stay awake at night and fast during the day as long as I live. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Are you the one who says that?” So I said to him: I said it. O Messenger of God, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You cannot do that, so fast and break your fast, sleep and stand up, and fast during the month.” Three days, for a good deed is rewarded ten times as much, and that is like fasting for an entire year.” I said: “I am able to do something better than that.” He said: “Fast a day.” And break your fast for two days. I said: I can do better than that, O Messenger of God. He said: Fast one day and break your fast the next. That is the fast of David. It is the most just of fasts.” I said: “I can do better than that.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No better than that.” Abdullah said. Bin Amr: Because I have accepted the three days that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, are more beloved to me than my family and my wealth."
"2675","Ahmad bin Bakkar told me, he said: Muhammad, who is Ibn Salamah, told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salamah Ibn Abdul Rahman, he said: I entered upon Abdullah Ibn Amr, and I said: What uncle, tell me about what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to you. He said: O son of my brother, I had agreed that I would strive very hard to the point that I said: I will fast forever, and I will recite the Qur’an every time. A day and a night. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, heard of that, so he came to me and entered my house and said: “I have been informed that you said: ‘I will fast. eternity, and He will surely recite the Qur’an.” I said: I have said that, O Messenger of God. He said: “Then do not do that. Fast for three days every month.” I said: I I am stronger than that. He said: “Then fast from Friday on Monday and Thursday.” I said: I am stronger than that. He said: “Fast the fast of David, peace be upon him, for it is the most equitable fasting in the eyes of God, a day when he fasts and a day when he breaks his fast. And if He promised, He would not He leaves behind, but when he meets him he does not flee.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2676","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated, saying: Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Shu`bah narrated, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Fayyad, he said: I heard Abu Iyad narrating On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fast one day during the month and you will have the reward of what remains.” He said: I I am able to do more than that. He said: “Fast for two days and you will have the reward of what remains.” He said: I am able to do more than that. He said: “Fast for three days and you will have the reward.” The reward for what remains.” He said: I am able to do more than that. He said: “Fast for four days and you will have the reward for what remains.” He said: I am able to do more than that. That is, he said: “The best fast in the eyes of God is the fasting of David, peace be upon him. He used to fast one day and break his fast the next.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2677","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala informed us, he said: Al-Mu`tamir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: Abu Al-Ala narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rabia, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, said: I mentioned fasting to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Fast one day out of every ten days, and you The reward for those nine days.” I said: I am stronger than that. He said: “Fast one day every nine days and you will have the reward for those eight days.” I said: I Stronger than that. He said: “Then fast one day every eight days and you will have the reward for those seven days.” I said: I am stronger than that. He said: Then he did not. Until then, he said: “Fast one day and break your fast the next.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2678","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Hammad informed. And Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Shuaib bin Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Fast a day and you will get the reward of ten,” so I said: Give me more, and he said: “ “Fast for two days and you will have the reward of nine.” I said: “Add me more.” He said: “Fast for three days and you will have the reward of eight.” Thabit said: So I was informed of that by Mutarrif. Ibn Abdullah, and he said: I only see that the work increases and the reward decreases. Abu Abdul Rahman said: Some of them increased over others. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2679","Muhammad ibn Ubaid al-Kufi told me, on the authority of Asbat ibn Muhammad Kufi, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Abu al-Abbas, On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “I have heard that you stay up all night and fast during the day?” I said: O Messenger of God, I wanted nothing but good by that. He said: “No one will fast who fasts forever, but I direct you to fasting forever, three days of the month.” I said. “O Messenger of God, I am able to do more than that.” He said: “Then fast for five days.” I said: I am able to do more than that. He said: “Then fast for ten days.” So I said: I am able to do more than that. He said: “So he fasted like the fast of David, and he used to fast one day and break his fast the other day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2680","Ali bin Al-Hussein narrated, saying: Umayyah bin Khalid Basri narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, he said: He narrated to me Abu Al-Abbas, who was a man from the Levant, was a poet, and was truthful, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to me: “You pray at night and fast during the day, and the one who fasts forever will not fast.” “Fast for three days every month.” I said: “Add me.” He said: “Fast for five days every month.” I said: “Add me.” He said: “The best fast is the fast of David. He fasted one day, broke his fast the next day, and did not flee if he met me.”"
"2681","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala reported, saying: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: Habib ibn Abi Thabit informed me, he said: I heard Abu Al-Abbas narrates, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “O Abdullah bin Amr, you are fasting eternity, and stay up all night, and when you do that, the eye will be relieved, and his soul will be comforted. No one fasts who has fasted forever. The perpetual fast is three days. Of the month is fasting for an entire lifetime.” I said: “I can bear more than that.” He said: “The fasting of David. He used to fast one day and break his fast one day and would not flee.” If he meets \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"2682","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, saying: Muhammad told us, meaning Ibn Ja`far Ghandar, saying: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu Abbas, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “Read the Qur’an in a month.” I said: I am able to More than that, he said: I kept asking him until, he said: “in five days”, and he said: “fast three days of the month”, I said: I I can bear more than that, so I kept asking him until he said: “Fast. The most beloved fast to God is the fast of David. He used to fast every day and break his fast.” \one day\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"2683","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, he said: Hajjaj told us, Ibn Jurayj said: I heard Ata’, that Abu Abbas the poet told him, that He heard Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas saying: News has reached the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that I will fast and pray during the night. He said: So he sent for him Or he met him and said: “Was I not informed that you fast, do not break your fast, and pray at night? So do not do that, for your eyes will have luck, and you will have luck for your soul. And for your family, fast and break your fast, pray and sleep, and fast one day every ten days, and you will receive the reward of nine. He said: I am stronger than That, O Messenger of God. He said: “Fast as David did then.” He said: How was David’s fast, O Prophet of God? He said: “He would fast one day and break his fast the next, and would not flee if he met someone.” He said: He said: Who can do this to me, O Prophet of God? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2684","Zakaria bin Yahya reported, he said: Wahb bin Baqiya told us, he said: Khaled reported, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, he said: I entered with your father Zaid Ali Abdullah bin Amr, and it happened that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned my fast to him. Then he came in to me and said: So I threw him a pillow stuffed with fiber, so he sat on the ground, so the pillow was between me and him, so he said: “Isn’t that enough for you? Three days every month? “I said: Increase it, O Messenger of God.” He said: “Five.” I said: O Messenger of God. He said: “Seven.” I said: O Messenger of God. He said: “Nine.” I said: O Messenger of God. He said: “Eleven.” I said: O Messenger of God. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There is no fast more than another.” David, for half a lifetime, fast one day and break the fast the next.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2685","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan Al-Masisi told me, he said: Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told me, on the authority of Ziyad bin Fayyad, he said: I heard Abu Iyadh say: Abdullah bin Amr said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “Fast one day of the month and you will have the reward of what remains.”"
"2686","Ali bin Hajar reported, he said: Ismail reported, he said: Muhammad bin Abi Harmala told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Dharr, He said: “My friend, may God bless him and grant him peace, advised me to do three things that I will never abandon, God willing: He advised me to pray the forenoon prayer, and to perform the Witr prayer before going to sleep. And by fasting three days of every month.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2687","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq al-Marwazi reported, saying: I heard my father. He said: Abu Hamza reported, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Hilal, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded me to do three things: sleeping on the odd-numbered prayer, and washing on Friday. And fasting three days of every month.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2688","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told me, he said: Abu Al-Nadr told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Hilal, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered me to “sleep on Witr prayers, wash on Friday, and fast for three days from \Every month\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"2689","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Abu Kamil told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Asim bin Bahdala, on the authority of a man, On the authority of Al-Aswad bin Hilal, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered me to perform the two rak’ahs of the forenoon prayer, and not to sleep except after praying the Witr prayer.” And fasting three days of every month. “The disagreement over Abu Uthman was mentioned in the report of Abu Hurairah regarding fasting three days of every month.”"
"2690","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Abdul Ala told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abu Uthman, that Abu Hurairah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The month of patience, and three days of every month are fasting forever.”"
"2691","Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Lani reported, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahim, who is Ibn Sulaiman, on the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Abu Dharr, who said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever fasts three days of the month should fast the entire time.” Then he said: God and His Messenger have spoken the truth in His Book. Whoever brings a good deed will get ten times it."
"2692","Muhammad bin Hatim reported, he said: Hibban told us, he said: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of a man, he said: Abu Dharr said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever fasts three days of every month has completed the fast of the month, or he has the right to fast the month.” Asim doubted (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2693","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Hind, that Mutarrif narrated to him, that Othman bin Abi Al-Aas said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Good fasting is three days of the month.” Zakaria bin Yahya, he said: Abu Musab told us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Hind, who said: Othman bin Abi Al-Aas, similarly mursal. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2694","Yusuf bin Saeed reported, saying: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Al-Hurr bin Sayyah, who said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He said: “He fasts three days of every month.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2695","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Al-Sabbah Al-Zaafrani reported, saying: Sa’id bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Al-Hurr bin Sayyah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to fast three days of every month: the Monday of the first of the month, then the following Thursday, then \The following Thursday\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"2696","Ali bin Muhammad reported, saying: Khalaf bin Tamim told us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Al-Hurr bin Sayyah, he said: I heard Hunaida Al-Khuza’i saying: I entered upon the Mother of the Believers and heard her saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to fast three days of every month: the first two. of the month, then Thursday, then the following Thursday.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2697","Abu Bakr bin Abi al-Nadr, the neighbor of Ibn al-Dawraqi, informed me, saying: Abu al-Nadr Hashim bin al-Qasim told me, he said: Abu Ishaq told us. Al-Ashja’i Kufi, on the authority of Amr bin Qais Al-Malali, on the authority of Al-Hurr bin Sayyah, on the authority of Hunaida bin Khalid Al-Khuza’i, on the authority of Hafsa Umm Believers, she said: There are four that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not abandon: “Fasting Ashura, the ten days, and the three days of every month. And two rak’ahs before lunch.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2698","Ahmad bin Yahya reported, on the authority of Abu Nu’aym, who said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Al-Hurr bin Sayyah, on the authority of Hunaydah bin Khalid, on the authority of His wife, on the authority of some of the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to fast the nine days of Dhul-Hijjah.” And the day of Ashura, and three days of every month, the first Monday and Thursday of the month.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2699","Muhammad ibn Uthman reported, saying: Abd al-Rahman told us, saying: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Hurr ibn al-Sayyah, on the authority of Hunaydah ibn Khalid, On the authority of his wife, on the authority of some of the wives of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, she said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to fast the ten days. And three days of every month, Monday and Thursday.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2700","I am Ibrahim bin Saeed Al-Jawhari. He said: Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Hunaida Al-Khuza’i, on the authority of his mother On the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “ordered fasting for three days, the first Thursday, Monday, and Monday.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2701","Mukhlid bin Al-Hasan reported, saying: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Zaid bin Abi Anisah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Jarir bin Abdullah Al-Bajli, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Fasting three days of every month is fasting throughout the year, and the white days are the morning of the thirteen and forty-five.” Ten and Fifteen “The disagreement over Musa bin Talha was mentioned in the report regarding fasting three days of the month.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2702","Muhammad bin Muammar Al-Basri, also called Al-Bahrani, reported: Hibban, who is Ibn Hilal Abu Habib, told us: Abu Habib told us: Awanah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Musa ibn Talha, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He had roasted a rabbit and placed it in his hands. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, caught it and did not eat. He ordered the people to eat. The Bedouin stopped, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “What prevents you from eating?” He said: “I fast three days of the month.” He said: “ “I was fasting, so fast the dawn.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2703","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rizmah reported, saying: Al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sam, on the authority of Musa ibn Talha, on the authority of Abu Dharr, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us to fast three days of the month, days “The eggs are thirteen, fourteen, and fifteen.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2704","Amr bin Yazid told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: I heard Yahya bin Sam, on the authority of Musa Ibn Talha, he said: I heard Abu Dharr in Al-Rabdhah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “If you fast three days of the month, then fast three days.” It means thirteen, fourteen, and fifteen.”"
"2705","Muhammad ibn Mansour told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Bayan ibn Bishr, on the authority of Musa ibn Talha, on the authority of Ibn al-Hutakiyyah, on the authority of Abu Dharr, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a man: “You must fast thirteen, fourteen, and fifteen days,” Abu Abd said. Al-Rahman: This is an error. This is not a hadith with a statement. Perhaps Sufyan said: We narrated two things, then the thousand was dropped, so a statement was made. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2706","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported, saying: Sufyan told us, he said: Two men told us Muhammad, who is the son of Abd al-Rahman, the client of the family of Talha, and a wise man. He is Ibn Jubayr, not strong, on the authority of Musa ibn Talha, on the authority of Ibn al-Hutakiyyah, on the authority of Abu Dharr, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “ordered A man who fasts thirteen days, fourteen days, and fifteen days.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Hakim bin Jubayr is not strong. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2707","Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim reported, on the authority of Bakr al-Kufi, the judge, on the authority of Isa, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of al-Hakam, on the authority of Musa ibn Talha, on the authority of Ibn Al-Hutakiyya, he said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he had with him a rabbit that he had roasted and baked, so he placed it in the hands of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. Then he said: I found blood on it, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It does not hurt, eat.” And he said to the Bedouins: “Eat.” He said: I am fasting. He said: “Fasting for what?” He said: Fasting three days of the month. He said: “If you are fasting, then you must wear Gharb al-Bayd for thirteen days. And fourteen, and fifteen.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The correct statement is on the authority of Abu Dharr, and it is similar to a speck falling from the book. It was said: Indeed, and God knows best (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2708","Amr ibn Yahya ibn al-Harith reported, saying: Al-Mu’afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Al-Qasim ibn Ma’n narrated to us, on the authority of Talha ibn Yahya ibn Talha, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, that a man brought a rabbit to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and it was as if the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, extended his hand to it. The one who brought it said: I saw blood on it, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, restrained his hand and ordered the people to eat, and he was in The people was a man who was a devotee, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “What’s the matter with you?” He said: I am fasting, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “So why not?” Three white ones: thirteen, fourteen, and fifteen.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2709","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Aliyah reported, saying: Ali told us, on the authority of Talha bin Yahya, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, he said: It was brought The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought a rabbit that a man had slaughtered. When he presented it to him, he said: O Messenger of God, I saw blood on it, so he left it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not eat it, and he said to whoever had it: “Eat, for if I craved it, I would eat it.” And a man was sitting, so he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Come closer and eat with the people.” He said: O Messenger of God, I am fasting. He said: “Then will the whites fast?” He said: What are they? He said: “Thirteen, fourteen, and fifteen.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2710","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala narrated, saying: Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, Anas bin Sirin narrated, on the authority of a man called: Abd al-Malik, narrating, On the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to order these three white days and say: ‘These are the fasts of the month.’” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2711","Muhammad ibn Hatim reported, he said: Hibban reported, he said: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Anas ibn Sirin, he said: I heard Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Al-Minhal narrates, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded them to fast three white days, and said: “And these are the fasts of the month.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2712","Muhammad ibn Muammar reported, he said: Hibban al-Basri told us, he said: Hammam told us, he said: Anas ibn Sirin told us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Sirin told me. Qudamah bin Milhan, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to command us to fast thirteen days on the white days.” And fourteen, and fifteen.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2713","Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Saif ibn Ubaid Allah narrated to us about the best of creation, he said: Al-Aswad ibn Shayban narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Nawfal ibn Abi Aqrab, on the authority of his father, said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about fasting, and he said: “Fast one day of the month.” He said: I said: O Messenger of God, increase me. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “Increase me, increase me. Fast two days of every month.” I said: O Messenger of God. By God, I find myself strong. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Give me more! I find myself strong.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, remained silent. He greeted me so much that I thought he was adding more to me. He said: “Fast three days of every month.”"
"2714","Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam reported, saying: Yazid bin Harun told us, saying: Al-Aswad bin Shayban reported, on the authority of Abu Nawfal bin Abi Aqrab, on the authority of his father, that he asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about fasting, and he said: “Fast one day every month,” so he increased it and said: By my father, you and my mother. I find myself strong, so give me more. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I find myself strong; I find myself strong.” He was almost unable to increase it, so he increased it and increased it, so he said: “Fast two days of every month.” Then he said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of God. You find me strong. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I find me strong. Accordingly, he said: “Fast three days of every month.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2715","Amr bin Ali told me, he said: Abu Dawud told me, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Ziyad bin Fayyad told me, he said: I heard Abu Iyad. He narrates, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “Fast one day on the first of the month and you will have the reward for what remains.”"
"2716","2719 Abdah bin Abdullah Al-Saffar Basri reported, saying: Abu Dawud Al-Hafari reported, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Saleel, on the authority of Mujibat Al-Bahili, on the authority of his uncle, he said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Do you know me, I am the one who came to you in the year He mentioned his beautiful body and said: I did not break my fast during the day except at night. He said: And whoever commands you to torture yourself, fast in the month of patience. And one day of the month.” He said: “I am stronger.” He said: “Fast for the month, and two days of the month.” He said: “I am stronger.” He said: “Fast for the month.” Patience and three days of the month.” He said: “I am stronger.” He said: “Fast in the Sacred Mosque and break your fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2717","Muhammad ibn Mansour and Al-Harith ibn Miskin narrated a reading of it and its pronunciation, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Yahya ibn Ja`dah, On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr Al-Qari, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah say: “I have not forbidden fasting on Friday, Muhammad and the Lord of the House.” \He forbade it\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"2718","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Jubayr bin Shaybah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abbad, he said: I asked Jabir bin Abdullah as he was circumambulating the Kaaba. “Did the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbid fasting on Friday?” He said: Yes, by the Lord of this. Al-Bayt mentions the disagreement over Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Jurayj in this hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2719","Yusuf bin Saeed Al-Masisi reported, saying: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abd al-Hamid bin Jubayr bin Shaybah informed me, that Muhammad bin Abbad bin Jaafar heard that he asked Jabir bin Abdullah while he was circumambulating the Kaaba: Did you hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? Is it forbidden to fast on Friday? He said: Yes, by the Lord of this House. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2720","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Muhammad bin Abbad bin Jafar told me, he said: I said By Jabir: Did you hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbidding the day of Friday to be singled out for fasting?” He said: “Yes, by the Lord of the Kaaba.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2721","Suleiman bin Salim Al-Balkhi reported, he said: Al-Nadr reported, he said: Ibn Jurayj reported, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abbad, that Jabir was asked about fasting on the day of Friday, and he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade you from setting it alone.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2722","Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abbad bin Jafar, on the authority of Jabir, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade fasting on Friday alone.” Mustawrid bin Abbad disagreed with him. Al-Hanayi (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2723","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala reported, saying: Khaled told us, he said: Mastur told us, he said: So-and-so bin Ja’far al-Makhzoumi told us, that a man met Abu Hurairah, while he was circumambulating the Kaaba, said: “Did you forbid people from fasting on Friday?” He said: No, by the Lord of the Kaaba, I did not forbid them. But the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade them “to mention disagreement over Muhammad ibn Sirin.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2724","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar Al-Kufi narrated, saying: Husayn Al-Ju’fi narrated to us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not single out Friday night for a night prayer, and do not single out Friday night.” “By fasting any of the days, unless it is during a fast that one of you fasts.”"
"2725","Abu Bakr bin Ali informed us, he said: Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Makhrami told us, he said: Al-Aswad bin Amir told us, he said: Israel told us On the authority of Asim, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Abu al-Darda’, do not single out the day “Friday is accompanied by fasting other than days, and Friday night is not distinguished by fasting other than nights.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2726","Ismail bin Masoud reported, he said: Bishr told us, he said: Sa`id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon Juwayriyah bint Al-Harith on Friday while she was fasting, and he said to her: “Be silent.” Yesterday? She said: No. He said: Do you want to fast tomorrow? She said: No. He said: So break your fast?"
"2727","Ibrahim bin Muhammad told me, meaning Al-Taimi, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, on the authority of Juwayriyah, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me while I was fasting on Friday. He said: “Did you fast yesterday?” I said: No. He said: “Will you fast tomorrow?” I said: No. He said: “Then break your fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2728","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria reported, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Do not single out Friday night for one of the nights’ fasting, and do not single out Friday for one of the days’ fasting.” “It must be during a fast that one of you is fasting.”"
"2729","Ahmad ibn Harb reported, saying: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “None of you should fast on Friday unless he fasts the day before or the day after.”"
"2730","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jafar told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: “None of you should fast on Friday unless he fasts before or after it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2731","Amr bin Ali reported, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shayban told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace. “He used to fast three days of every month, and I rarely saw him break his fast on Friday.”"
"2732","Hussein bin Mansour reported, saying: Mubashir bin Ismail told us, saying: Hassan bin Nuh told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Busr, that he said: Do you see this hand? I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I heard him say: “Do not fast on the Sabbath except an obligatory fast. If none of you finds anything except The bark of a tree, let him break his fast with it.”"
"2733","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Ibn Abdullah bin Busr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his paternal aunt. The deaf sister of Busr said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade fasting on the Saturday, and he said: “If any of you finds nothing but a stick... green, let him break his fast.”"
"2734","Ali bin Khashram reported, he said: Jesus reported, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Khalid bin Ma’dan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Busr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: “Do not fast on Saturdays except for what is obligatory for you.”"
"2735","Muhammad bin Ismail told me, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Asbagh is Ibn Zaid, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Khalid bin Ma’dan, he said Abdullah bin Busr told me that his sister, called the deaf woman, told him that she heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “No.” “You shall fast on the Sabbath, except for what is obligatory for you, and if any of you finds nothing but a stalk of grapes or the bark of a tree, let him chew it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2736","Humayd bin Masada reported, on the authority of Sufyan bin Habib, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Khalid bin Ma’dan, then he mentioned a word that meant it, on the authority of Abd Allah ibn Busr, on the authority of his sister, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not fast on the Sabbath except what has been made obligatory for you. “If any of you finds anything but the bark of a grape or the stick of a tree, let him chew it.”"
"2737","Nusayr bin Al-Faraj told me: It was written about him with Al-Thaghr, and his nickname is Hamzah. He said: Abdul-Malik bin Al-Sabbah told us, he said: He told us Thawr, on the authority of Khaled, who is Ibn Ma’dan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Busr, on the authority of his sister, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No “You shall fast on the Sabbath, except for what is obligatory upon you. If any of you finds anything other than a stalk of grapes or the bark of a tree, let him chew it.”"
"2738","Saeed bin Amr told us, he said: Baqiya told us, he said: Thawr told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Maadan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Busr, on the authority of his paternal aunt. Al-Samma’a, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do not fast on the Sabbath except what is obligatory for you, even if none of you finds anything except a stick of grapes or “The bark of a tree, let him chew it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2739","I am Amr bin Othman. He said: Baqiya told us. He said: Al-Zubaidi told me. He said: Luqman bin Amir told me, on the authority of Amer bin Jashib, on the authority of Khalid bin Maadan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Busr, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not fast on the Sabbath except on what is required upon you, and if any of you finds nothing but the bark of a tree, let him break his fast.”"
"2740","Imran bin Bakkar told us, he said: Al-Rabi’ bin Rawh told us, he said: Muhammad bin Harb told us, he said: Al-Zubaidi told us, on the authority of Al-Fudayl bin Fadala, on the authority of Abdullah bin Busr, on the authority of his deaf aunt, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Do not fast on the day of The Sabbath, except for what is obligatory, upon you, even if none of you breaks the fast except on the bark of a tree.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I narrated on the authority of Ibn Salem, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi said: Al-Fudayl bin Fadalah told us that Khaled bin Ma’dan narrated to him, that Abdullah bin Busr narrated to him that he heard his father, He says: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade fasting on Saturdays,” and the like. Imran told us, he said: Abu Taqi told us, He said: Ibn Salem narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, he said: Al-Fudayl bin Fadhalah narrated to us, that Khalid bin Ma’dan narrated to him, that Abdullah bin He told him a secret that he had heard from his father that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade fasting on the Sabbath, and said: “If he does not find... . . “And he mentioned the hadith. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This Abu Taqi is weak and nothing, but I only included it for the reason of disagreement. Sa`id bin Amr, he said: Baqiyya told us, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Luqman bin Amir, on the authority of Khaled bin Ma’dan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Basr, on the authority of His deaf paternal aunt, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was similar to him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2741","Imran bin Bakkar told us, he said: Yazid bin Abdul Rabbo told us, he said: Baqiyya told us, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Aamir bin Jashib, on the authority of Khalid bin Maadan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Busr, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do not fast on the Sabbath except what has been made obligatory for you.” “And if any of you finds nothing but the bark of a tree, let him break his fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2742","Muhammad bin Wahb told me, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Abu Abdul Rahim told me, on the authority of Al-Ala, on the authority of Dawud bin Ubaid. By God, on the authority of Khalid bin Maadan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Busr, on the authority of his deaf sister, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Do not fast on the Sabbath except what has been made obligatory for you, and if any of you finds anything other than the bark of a tree, let him chew it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2743","Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Muhammad reported on the authority of Ishaq bin Ibrahim, who said: Muawiyah bin Yahya Abu Muti’ told us, he said: Tell me Artat, he said: I heard Abu Amer, he said: I heard Thuban, the servant of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was asked about fasting on Saturdays, and he said: Ask Abdullah bin Busr. He said: He was asked and he said: “Fasting the Sabbath is neither for you nor against you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2744","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman reported, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, saying: Al-Layth bin Sa’d told me, and someone else before him mentioned, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib. On the authority of Abu Al-Khair, on the authority of Hudhayfah Al-Barqi, on the authority of Junadat Al-Azdi, that eight people entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He was the eighth of them, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought food to them on a Friday, and he said: “Eat.” They said: “Fasting.” He said: “You fast.” Yesterday? They said: No. He said: Tomorrow? They said: No, he said: “Then break your fast.” Ahmad bin Bakkar told me, he said: Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, On the authority of Hudhayfah al-Azdi, on the authority of Junadat al-Azdi, he said: I entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I was the eighth of seven of my Azd people. So he mentioned something similar (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2745","Kathir ibn Ubaid al-Homsi reported, saying: Baqiya ibn al-Walid narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Omar. He is Ibn Ali, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Kurayb, that Ibn Abbas was sent to Umm Salamah and to Aisha, asking them: What was the Messenger of God? May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he likes to fast on a number of days, so they said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not die so much of his fasting on a day. Saturday and Sunday, and he says: “They are holidays for the People of the Book, so we like to differ from them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2746","Muhammad bin Hatim Al-Marwazi reported, he said: Hibban reported, he said: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Omar bin Ali, he said: He told me My father, on the authority of Kurayb, he said: Ibn Abbas sent me and some of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Umm Salamah: What day was the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He, peace and blessings be upon him, is the one who fasts the most? She said: On Saturday and Sunday, they denounced me and thought that I had not memorized it, so they turned me away. She said: Like that, so I told them, so they stood up. All of them, and they said: We have sent to you about such-and-such. Then this man claimed that you said such-and-such. She said: He spoke the truth. He was the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he fasts on Saturday and Sunday the most of the days he fasts, and he says: “They are a holiday for the polytheists, so I love \to disagree with them\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"2747","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, he said: Mahdi bin Maymun told us, on the authority of Ghaylan bin Jarir, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Ma`abad al-Zamani, on the authority of Abu Qatada, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about fasting on Mondays. He said: “It is the day on which I was born.” And the day on which it was revealed to me.”"
"2748","Abu Dawud Al-Harrani reported, he said: ‘Arim told us, he said: Thabit told us, he said: Hilal, who is Ibn Khabab, told us, on the authority of one of the ‘Arifs. Quraysh, he said: My father told me that he heard from people, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Whoever fasts Ramadan, Shawwal, and Wednesday And on Thursday he entered Paradise.”"
"2749","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, and I am Ahmed bin Yahya, they said: Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: Harun bin Salman told us, he said: he told me Muslim bin Abdullah Al-Qurashi said that his father told him that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fast Ramadan and the following Ramadan and every day of Ramadan.” Wednesday and Thursday, then you have fasted forever.” And Ibrahim said: Muslim bin Ubaid Allah (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2750","Abdah bin Abdullah Al-Basri reported, saying: Zaid, who was Ibn Hubab, reported, saying: Harun bin Salman Abu Musa, Amr’s servant, told me. Bin Harith, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Muslim Al-Qurashi told me, on the authority of his father, he said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about fasting three days. He said: “Fast the month of Ramadan and the following, and on Wednesday and Thursday, then you fasted for a lifetime and broke your fast.”"
"2751","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani al-Basri reported, on the authority of Khalid, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Umar ibn al-Hakam ibn Thawban, that The servant of Qudamah bin Mazun narrated to him that the servant of Osama said: Osama used to ride to his property in Wadi al-Qura and fast on the day of Monday and Thursday, I said to him: Do you fast while traveling, since you have grown up? He said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fasting on Mondays and Thursdays. He said: “Deeds are presented on Mondays and Thursdays.” Ubaid Allah bin Saeed Al-Sarkhasi reported, saying: Muadh bin Hisham Al-Dastawai told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said Omar ibn Abd al-Hakam ibn Thawban narrated to me, that the client of Qudamah ibn Mad’un narrated to him, that the client of Usama ibn Zayd narrated to him, that Osama was riding for money that had the basis of the hadith. Ubayd Allah ibn Fadhalah informed me, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri informed me, he said: Muawiyah ibn Salam ibn Abi Salam told us, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Abi Kathir, he said: The servant of Qudamah Ibn Mazun told me that the servant of Usama Ibn Zayd told him that Usama Ibn Zayd was He fasts on Mondays and Thursdays and the like. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu Salam, his name is Mamtur. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2752","Mahmoud bin Khalid told me, he said: Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Abu Amr, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of a servant of Usama bin Zaid, that Usama bin Zaid He used to fast on Mondays and Thursdays, and it is reported that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to fast them as well.”"
"2753","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Habib bin Al-Shahid Al-Basri reported, saying: Yahya bin Al-Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Musayyab. Ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Sawa al-Khuza’i, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to fast on Mondays and Thursdays.”"
"2754","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria reported, saying: Husayn told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Hafsa, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, May God bless him and grant him peace, he fasts on Mondays and Thursdays.”"
"2755","Ismail bin Masoud Al-Basri reported, saying: Khalid told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdullah bin Qariz, on the authority of Abu Ubaid, he said: I witnessed Ali and Uthman on the Day of Sacrifice and Breakfast praying, then they went away and reminded the people, and I heard them say: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade fasting on these two days.”"
"2756","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Sufyan reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Ubaid, the client of bin Azhar, he said: I witnessed the Eid with Omar bin The preacher began with prayer before the sermon, then said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade fasting on these two days. The Day of Fitr is the day on which you break your fast, and as for the Day of Al-Adha, it is the day of your ritual ritual.”"
"2757","Muhammad ibn Qudamah Al-Musaysi told me, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Sahm, on the authority of Qaza’ah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No fasting on the day of Eid.” He mentioned the disagreement over Qatada in this hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2758","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported, saying: Ibn Bī Adiy told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Qaza’ah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, “that The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade fasting on the Day of Breakfast and the Day of Sacrifice.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2759","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed reported, saying: Muadh bin Hisham reported, saying: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Qaza’ah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, he said “The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade fasting on the Day of Breakfast and the Day of Sacrifice.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2760","Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Yazid told us, he is the son of Zuray’, he said: Hisham told us, he said: Qatada told us, on the authority of Qaza’ah, on the authority of Abu Saeed, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade fasting on two days: fasting the Day of Sacrifice and the Day of Breaking the fast.”"
"2761","Zakaria bin Yahya reported, he said: Abd al-Ala told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, and on the authority of Bishr ibn Harb. On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade fasting on the Day of Breaking the fast and the Day of Sacrifice,” Abu Abd said. Al-Rahman: Bishr ibn Harb is weak, but we only brought him out for the reason of the hadith and the truth is the hadith of Saeed and Hisham, and God knows best."
"2762","Muhammad ibn Salamah and al-Harith ibn Miskin reported a recitation by him while I was listening, and the pronunciation was his, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, Malik told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade fasting for two days on the Al-Fitr and the Day of Eid Al-Adha (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2763","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed reported, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Mansour told me, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Iyas bin Harmala, on the authority of Abu Qatada, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Fasting Ashura atones for the previous year, and fasting Arafat atones for the past two years.” And the future.” Mahmoud bin Ghaylan reported, saying: Abd al-Razzaq told us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Harmala ibn Iyas, on the authority of Abu Qatada, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Likewise. Issa bin Muhammad al-Ramli reported to Abu Umair, he said: Al-Faryabi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Al-Khalil, on the authority of Harmala ibn Iyas, on the authority of Abu Qatada, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, something similar. I am Mahmoud bin Ghaylan, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Al-Khalil, on the authority of Harmala, on the authority of A servant of Abu Qatada, he said: Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Thawri, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Al-Khalil, on the authority of Harmala ibn Iyas, on the authority of A servant of Abu Qatada, on the authority of Abu Qatada, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, similar to it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2764","Musa bin Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi reported to al-Kufi, saying: Husayn bin Ali al-Jufi’i told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Al-Khalil, on the authority of Iyas bin Harmala Al-Sadusi, on the authority of Abu Qatada, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fasting the Day of Arafah is an expiation “Two years, a year before it and a year after it, and fasting on the day of Ashura is atonement for a year.”"
"2765","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria reported, saying: Ishaq bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Mansour, who said: I and Mujahid went to my father. Al-Khalil mentioned, on the authority of Abu Qatada, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Fasting Arafat is an expiation for a year before it and a year after it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2766","I am Muhammad bin Al-Musaffa. He said: Muawiyah bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Hisham, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Al-Khalil, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fasting Arafat is an expiation for two years, a previous year and a year ago.” In the future, fasting on Ashura is atonement for a year.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2767","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri reported, saying: Sufyan reported, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Abu Qaza’ah, on the authority of Abu al-Khalil, on the authority of Abu Harmala, on the authority of Abu Qatada, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Fasting on the day of Ashura expiates the Sunnah, and fasting on the day of Arafah expiates The year and the following year.” Masoud bin Juwayriyah Al-Mawsili, Al-Hasan bin Issa, and Harun bin Abdullah reported, saying: Sufyan reported, on the authority of Dawud bin Shabour, on the authority of Abu Qaza’ah, on the authority of Abu al-Khalil, on the authority of Abu Harmala, on the authority of Abu Qatada, and the like. Harun said in his hadith: We heard it from Dawud. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2768","Muhammad bin Ubayd Allah told me, he said: Al-Hasan bin Bishr told me, he said: Zuhayr told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abu Al-Khalil, on the authority of Abu Harmala, on the authority of Abu Qatada, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fasting Ashura is an expiation for a year, and fasting Arafah is an expiation.” “Two years past and future.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Al-Hasan bin Bishr is not, according to us, strong in hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2769","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid reported, on the authority of his father, he said: Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: Abu Al-Khalil told me, on the authority of Harmala Ibn Iyas, on the authority of Abu Qatada, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fasting the day of Arafat is equivalent to two years, and fasting the day of Ashura \Equivalent to a year.\"" Amr bin Ali told us"
"2770","Hajib bin Sulayman al-Munbiji reported, on the authority of Waki`, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Ata`, on the authority of Abu al-Khalil, on the authority of Abu Qatada, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Fasting Ashura is atonement for one year, and fasting Arafat is atonement for two years: past and future.” Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam reported, saying: Muhammad bin Rabi’ah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu al-Khalil, on the authority of Abu Qatada, something similar. Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan Al-Masisi told me, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata’ told me, on the authority of Abu Al-Khalil, On the authority of Abu Qatada. Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal reported, he said: My father told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ka’b and the like. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2771","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jaafar told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Ghaylan bin Jarir, he heard Abdullah bin Ma’bad, On the authority of Abu Qatada, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about fasting on the Day of Arafat. He said: “It expiates the past year and the following year.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is the best hadith on this subject in my opinion, and God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2772","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Al-Miswar Al-Zuhri Al-Basri reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, he said: I came to Ibn Abbas on the day of Arafat and found him eating pomegranates, so he said: “Come and eat. Perhaps you are fasting. Indeed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, did not fast this day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2773","Ahmad bin Harb told Al-Mawsili, brother of Ali bin Harb, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, he said: I came to Ibn Abbas was at Arafat while he was eating pomegranates and said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, broke his fast at Arafat, so Umm al-Fadl sent milk and he drank it.” \"" 2774"""""
"2774","Ziyad ibn Ayyub al-Dalluwayh informed me, saying: Isma'il narrated to us, saying: Ayyub narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) broke his fast at 'Arafah, and Umm al-Fadl sent him some milk, and he drank it."""""
"2775","Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Al-Qawariri told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, that Ibn Abbas He broke his fast at Arafat. A pomegranate was brought to him and he ate. He said: Umm al-Fadl told me, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, broke his fast at Arafat. She brought him With milk, he drank it.”"
"2776","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, “that Ibn Abbas broke his fast at Arafat and was brought with a pomegranate.” \So he ate it\"""""""
"2777","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Ahmad bin Issa told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, and Sa`id, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he broke his fast at Arafat. A pomegranate was brought to him and he ate it, and he said: Umm al-Fadl told me that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, broke his fast at Arafat. He was brought milk and he drank it. “Ibrahim bin Yaqoub Al-Jawzjani told me, saying: Abu Al-Nu’man and Sulayman bin Harb told us, saying: Hammad bin Zayd told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, that Ibn Abbas, like him, was equal. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2778","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim reported, saying: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata’ told me, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he called his brother Ubaidullah went to food on the day of Arafat, and he said: I am fasting, and he said: You are the people of a household who should be followed by example. I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. A milkmaid was brought with milk on this day and he drank.”"
"2779","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, he said: Hajjaj told us, Ibn Jurayj said: Ata’ said: Abdullah bin Abbas called Al-Fadl bin Abbas, On the day of Arafat, he went to eat and said: “I am fasting.” Abdullah said, “Do not fast, for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “milk milk was brought to him containing milk.” on the Day of Arafat and drink from it.” Do not fast, for the people are waiting for you. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2780","Ishaq bin Mansour reported to Al-Kusaj Maruzi, he said: Abdul-Rahman reported, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu Al-Sawda, He said: I asked Ibn Umar, “about fasting on the Day of Arafat, but he forbade me.”"
"2781","Amr bin Ali reported, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan and Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, “Omar forbade fasting on the Day of Arafat.”"
"2782","Ahmad bin Uthman Abu Al-Jawza Basri narrated, saying: Al-Mu’amil bin Ismail narrated to us with many errors, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Nafi’, said: Ibn Umar was asked about fasting on the day of Arafah at Arafat. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not fast on it. “peace be upon him, nor Abu Bakr, nor Omar, nor Othman.”"
"2783","Ali bin Hajar reported, saying: Sufyan and Ismail reported, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who was asked about fasting on the day of Arafat, and he said: I performed Hajj with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, but he did not fast it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2784","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala reported, saying: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn Umar. He was asked about fasting on the Day of Arafat, and he said: “I performed Hajj with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but he did not fast it, and with Abu Bakr he did not fast.” He fasted it, and he was with Omar and he did not fast it, and he was with Othman and he did not fast it, and I do not fast it, and I do not command or forbid you to fast it. If you wish, then fast. If you wish, do not fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2785","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala reported, saying: Al-Mu`tamir told us, saying: I read to Fudayl, on the authority of Abu Hariz, that he heard Saeed bin Jubayr, saying: A man asked Abdullah bin Omar about fasting on the Day of Arafat. He said: “While we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, we equated it with fasting for a year.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Abu Jarir is not strong, and his name is Abdullah bin Hussein Qadi Sijistan, and this is an objectionable hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2786","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar reported, he said: Zaid told us, he said: Musa bin Ali told me, he said: I heard my father, saying: I heard Uqba bin Amir. He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Day of Arafat, the Day of Sacrifice, and the three days of Tashreeq according to the people of Islam. \Eating and drinking\"""""""
"2787","Suleiman bin Ma’bad Al-Maruzi reported, saying: Sulayman bin Harb told us, saying: Hawshab bin Aqeel told us, on the authority of Mahdi Al-Hijri, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade fasting on the Day of Arafah at Arafat.”"
"2788","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, he said: Hawshab bin Aqeel told us, on the authority of Mahdi al-Abdi, he said: he told me and mentioned Ikrimah said: I went to Abu Hurairah and asked him about fasting at Arafat, and he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade Fasting on the Day of Arafat with Arafat"
"2789","Ishaq bin Mansour reported, saying: Abd al-Rahman reported, saying: Hawshab and Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr said: “Umar forbade fasting on the Day of Arafat.”"
"2790","Al-Hussein bin Issa reported, saying: Azhar told us, then he mentioned a word that means, Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Jubayr, that Ibn Umar He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade fasting on the Day of Sacrifice.”"
"2791","Ziyad bin Ayyub told me, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Bishr reported, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: When The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Medina and found the Jews fasting on the day of Ashura. They were asked about that, and they said: This is the day on which God made Moses appear victorious, and the children of Israel were defeated by Pharaoh, and we fasted in honor of him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “We He is more worthy of Moses than you and commanded his fasting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2792","Muhammad bin Mansour reported, saying: Sufyan told us, he said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Ibn Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Medina and found the Jews fasting on the day of Ashura. He asked them: “What is this?” They said: “A day of Ashura.” God saved Moses on that day and drowned the people of Pharaoh on that day, so Moses fasted in thanksgiving to God, as we fast on that day. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: We are more deserving of Moses, and he was more deserving of his fasting, so he fasted and commanded his fasting.” Ismail bin Yaqoub Al-Harabi Al-Subaihi reported, saying: Ibn Musa, who is Ibn Ayan, told us, saying: My father told us, on the authority of Al-Harith, meaning Ibn Umair, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas and the like. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2793","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, that Arak told him, that Urwa told him, about Aisha, that the Quraysh used to fast on Ashura in the pre-Islamic era, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered his fasting, and when Ramadan was imposed, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever wants, let him fast from it, and whoever wants, let him break his fast.”"
"2794","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed reported, saying: Yahya told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “It was the day of Ashura. It was a day that the Quraysh fasted in the pre-Islamic era, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to fast on it. When he came to Medina, he fasted and ordered that he fast. Then the fast of Ramadan came, and Ramadan was the obligatory fast, so whoever wished may fast, meaning Ashura, and whoever wished may leave it.”"
"2795","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed told me, he said: My father told us, he said: Shuaib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Urwa told me, on the authority of Aisha said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to order the fasting of Ashura before Ramadan was imposed. When Ramadan was imposed, it was Whoever wishes may fast Ashura, and whoever wishes may break his fast.”"
"2796","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he was mentioned with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day Ashura, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It was a day that the people of pre-Islamic times fasted, so whoever among you would like to fast it, let him fast it.” And whoever hates it, let him leave it.”"
"2797","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Waki` reported, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Mukhaymara, on the authority of Abu Ammar. On the authority of Qais bin Saad, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered us to fast on Ashura before Ramadan came. He neither commanded us nor forbade us.”"
"2798","Ismail bin Masoud reported, he said: Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Zuray’, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Utaiba, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Mukhaymira, on the authority of Amr ibn Shurahbil, on the authority of Qays ibn Saad, who said: “We used to fast on the day of Ashura and pay zakat al-fitr, so when it was revealed... “Ramadan, and the zakat was revealed, we were not commanded to it, nor were we forbidden from it, but we used to do it.”"
"2799","Omar bin Ibrahim Abu Al-Adhaan told us, he said: Ali bin Shuaib told us, he said: Abu Al-Nadr told us, he said: Al-Ashja’i told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah, like: “We used to fast Ashura, but when Ramadan came, we were not commanded to fast.” And We did not forbid it, but we used to do it.”"
"2800","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, saying: Muhammad told us, saying: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Al-Ash’ath ibn Qays entered upon Abdullah on the day of Ashura while he was eating. He said: Come closer and eat. He said: I am fasting. Then he said: Abdullah. This was a day we fasted before... Ramadan, so if you want to eat, come and feed.” Mention of the disagreement over Amara bin Umair in the report of Abdullah bin Masoud regarding fasting on the day of Ramadan. Ashura (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2801","Muhammad bin Al-Ala reported, saying: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, who said: He entered Al-Ash'ath bin Qais met Abdullah bin Masoud on the day of Ashura while he was having lunch, and Abdullah said to him: O Abu Muhammad, come closer, and he said: I He is fasting, today is the day of Ashura. He said: Do you know what the day of Ashura was? He said: What was it? He said, “A day on which the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to fast before Ramadan came, but when Ramadan came, he abandoned it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2802","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Zubaid told me, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Qays bin Al-Sakan: Al-Ash’ath ibn Qays entered upon Abdullah on the day of Ashura while he was eating, and said: Come closer and eat. He said: I am fasting. He said: We were We fast it and then leave it.”"
"2803","Ahmad ibn Harb reported, saying: Ibn Ulayya told us, on the authority of Mansour ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Alqamah, he said: “I came to Ibn Masoud, from Ramadan to Ramadan, there was not a day on which I did not go to him, and I did not see him on a fasting day or on the day of Ashura.”"
"2804","Al-Hussein bin Harith reported, saying: Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abu Umays, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, on the authority of Abu Musa, He said: The day of Ashura was a day on which the Jews fasted and considered it a holiday. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Medina, he was informed of that. Then he said: “So fast on it you.” A neck followed him."
"2805","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Abu Al-Walid told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Raqbah, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, On the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, he said: The day of Ashura was a holiday for the people of Yathrib in which women wore their badges, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And he said: “They differ from them, so fast.”"
